* You can also add additional features to the pagination, such as displaying the current page number and the total number of pages. For example, you can add a `totalPages` property to the component and calculate it based on the total number of items and the number of items per page:
```
totalPages = 0;

getData(page: number) {
  this.http.get(`http://localhost:5000/data?page=${page}`)
    .pipe(
      catchError(error => {
        console.error(error);
        alert('An error occurred while retrieving the data. Please try again.');
        return [];
      })
    )
    .subscribe(response => {
      this.data = response;

      // Calculate the total number of pages
      this.totalPages = Math.ceil(this.data.length / 100);

      // Check if the current page is the last page of data
      if (this.data.length < 100) {
        this.lastPage = true;
      } else {
        this.lastPage = false;
      }

      // Check if the current page is the first page of data
      if (this.currentPage == 1) {
        this.firstPage = true;
      } else {
        this.firstPage = false;
      }
    });
}
```
* In the Angular template, you can display the current page number and the total number of pages:
```
<div>
  <p>Page {{ currentPage }} of {{ totalPages }}</p>
  <button (click)="previousPage()" [disabled]="firstPage">Previous</button>
  <button (click)="nextPage()" [disabled]="lastPage">Next</button>
</div>
```
