```
<div>
  <p>Page {{ currentPage }} of {{ totalPages }}</p>
  <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="pageInput" />
  <button (click)="goToPage()">Go</button>
  <button (click)="previousPage()" [disabled]="firstPage">Previous</button>
  <button (click)="nextPage()" [disabled]="lastPage">Next</button>
</div>
```
* In the component, you can add a `pageInput` property and a `goToPage()` method to handle the user's input:
```
pageInput = 1;

goToPage() {
  const page = parseInt(this.pageInput);
  if (page >= 1 && page <= this.totalPages) {
    this.currentPage = page;
    this.getData(this.currentPage);
  } else {
    alert('Please enter a valid page number.');
  }
}
```
